turn_origin provenance for Hermes Agent v0.21.5 hook payloads
============================================================

Built and tested against Hermes Agent v0.21.5. Hermes Agent is a Nous Research project;
this patch is an independent, minimal integration that this repository (a standalone plugin
project) needs in order to know whether a turn came from a real human. It contains no
upstream source beyond the few context lines a unified diff requires, and it claims no
affiliation with or authorship of the upstream project.

Why it exists
-------------
The ``pre_api_request`` hook fires for every provider request the agent makes, including
requests that do not belong to a human turn: gateway self-injected notifications, compaction
continuations, background-review forks, delegated subagents, CLI one-shot runs, cron jobs and
curator runs. A hook payload that carries only ``platform`` cannot separate those from a human
message, because a fork or notification inherits the platform label of the session it came
from (a background review of a Feishu conversation reports ``platform=feishu``).

What the patch adds
-------------------
A structural, per-turn ``turn_origin`` label, decided by the core *before* the request is
assembled, and exposed in the ``pre_api_request`` payload:

* new module ``agent/turn_origin.py`` — the closed vocabulary and the classifier;
* ``agent/conversation_loop.py`` — classify once at turn setup;
* ``agent/turn_api_request.py`` — put ``turn_origin`` into the hook payload;
* ``gateway/run_turn_runner.py`` — set the structural hint for the turn being dispatched;
* ``hermes_cli/oneshot.py`` — stamp CLI one-shot runs.

Vocabulary: ``user``, ``internal_notification``, ``compaction_continuation``,
``background_review``, ``subagent``, ``oneshot``, ``cron``, ``curator``, ``api_server``,
``unknown``. The decision uses Hermes' own turn metadata only — never message text — and
**fails closed to ``unknown``**: a payload with no ``turn_origin`` means "not eligible", so a
Hermes upgrade that drops this integration cannot silently restore unconditional routing
(the plugin rejects a missing label).

Apply
-----
    patch -p1 --dry-run < patches/hermes-v0.21.5-turn-origin.patch      # from the Hermes root
    patch -p1 < patches/hermes-v0.21.5-turn-origin.patch

Then restart the gateway and verify with::

    python3 tools/check_turn_origin_patch.py --hermes-root /path/to/hermes

Uninstall: reverse the patch (``patch -R -p1``) and delete ``agent/turn_origin.py``; the plugin
then rejects every turn and routing stays inert.

diff --git a/agent/turn_origin.py b/agent/turn_origin.py
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/agent/turn_origin.py
+"""Turn-origin classification for hook payloads.
+
+JEV-TURN-ORIGIN-PATCH v0.21.5 — added for the v0.2.0 human-turn provenance boundary.
+
+Why
+---
+``pre_api_request`` fires for every provider request the agent makes, including requests that do
+not belong to a real user turn: gateway self-injected notifications, compaction continuations,
+background-review forks, delegated subagents, CLI oneshot runs, cron jobs and curator runs.
+Consumers that must only ever see human turns need a structural, authoritative origin — decided
+by the core before the request is built — instead of guessing from the message text.
+
+Contract
+--------
+* ``ORIGINS`` is the closed set of values; anything else (or a missing value) is ``unknown``.
+* The value is decided from Hermes' own turn metadata only (``agent.platform``, the persisted
+  user-row display kind, Hermes' compaction-carrier classifier, and the upstream
+  ``agent._turn_origin`` fork tag). Message text is never used to decide ``user``.
+* Fail-closed: ``unknown`` is the fallback. ``user`` is only ever reported when the gateway
+  dispatch explicitly identified a real inbound platform message (hint) — never by default.
+* ``assign()`` runs once per turn, before any API request is assembled, so the value is already
+  final when ``pre_api_request`` fires.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import logging
+
+logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
+
+# JEV-TURN-ORIGIN-PATCH v0.21.5 (marker consumed by tools/check_turn_origin_patch.py)
+ORIGINS = (
+    "user",
+    "internal_notification",
+    "compaction_continuation",
+    "background_review",
+    "subagent",
+    "oneshot",
+    "cron",
+    "curator",
+    "api_server",
+    "unknown",
+)
+
+UNKNOWN = "unknown"
+
+#: Per-turn value read by hook payload builders.
+ATTR = "turn_origin"
+#: Per-turn hint set by the gateway right before it dispatches the turn ("user" / internal kind).
+HINT_ATTR = "_turn_origin_hint"
+#: Upstream fork tag (agent/background_review.py) — authoritative when present.
+UPSTREAM_ATTR = "_turn_origin"
+
+# platform -> origin, for entry points that already identify themselves structurally.
+PLATFORM_ORIGINS = {
+    "subagent": "subagent",
+    "cron": "cron",
+    "curator": "curator",
+    "api_server": "api_server",
+}
+
+
+def normalize(value) -> str:
+    """Return a valid origin string, or ``unknown`` (never guesses ``user``)."""
+    if isinstance(value, str):
+        v = value.strip().lower()
+        if v in ORIGINS:
+            return v
+    return UNKNOWN
+
+
+def _platform(agent) -> str:
+    try:
+        return str(getattr(agent, "platform", "") or "").strip().lower()
+    except Exception:
+        return ""
+
+
+def _is_compaction_carrier(user_message) -> bool:
+    """True when the turn's user message is a compaction handoff (Hermes' own classifier)."""
+    try:
+        from agent.context_compressor import is_compaction_summary_message
+
+        if isinstance(user_message, dict):
+            return bool(is_compaction_summary_message(user_message))
+        if isinstance(user_message, str):
+            return bool(is_compaction_summary_message({"role": "user", "content": user_message}))
+    except Exception:
+        return False
+    return False
+
+
+def classify(agent, *, persist_user_display_kind=None, user_message=None) -> str:
+    """Decide this turn's origin from structural metadata. Never inspects text to say ``user``."""
+    # 1. upstream fork tag / explicit stamp (background review, oneshot, ...)
+    sticky = normalize(getattr(agent, UPSTREAM_ATTR, None))
+    if sticky != UNKNOWN:
+        return sticky
+    # 2. platform already identifies the entry point
+    platform_origin = PLATFORM_ORIGINS.get(_platform(agent))
+    if platform_origin:
+        return platform_origin
+    # 3. compaction continuation (carrier message rather than a fresh human message)
+    if _is_compaction_carrier(user_message):
+        return "compaction_continuation"
+    # 4. gateway hint (structural: the dispatch knew whether the event was self-injected)
+    hint = normalize(getattr(agent, HINT_ATTR, None))
+    if hint != UNKNOWN:
+        return hint
+    # 5. fail-closed
+    return UNKNOWN
+
+
+def assign(agent, *, persist_user_display_kind=None, user_message=None) -> str:
+    """Stamp ``agent.turn_origin`` for this turn. Never raises; always ends in a valid origin."""
+    origin = UNKNOWN
+    try:
+        origin = classify(agent, persist_user_display_kind=persist_user_display_kind,
+                          user_message=user_message)
+    except Exception:
+        logger.debug("turn-origin classification failed; reporting unknown", exc_info=True)
+        origin = UNKNOWN
+    try:
+        setattr(agent, ATTR, origin)
+    except Exception:
+        pass
+    try:
+        # Single-use: a hint must never leak into a later turn of the same agent object.
+        delattr(agent, HINT_ATTR)
+    except Exception:
+        pass
+    return origin
+
+
+def stamp(agent, origin: str) -> str:
+    """Entry-point stamp (fork/oneshot): authoritative for that agent from now on."""
+    value = normalize(origin)
+    try:
+        setattr(agent, UPSTREAM_ATTR, value)
+    except Exception:
+        pass
+    return value
+
+
+def current(agent) -> str:
+    """Read this turn's origin for a hook payload. Fail-closed to ``unknown``."""
+    value = normalize(getattr(agent, ATTR, None))
+    if value != UNKNOWN:
+        return value
+    # A payload may be built before assign() ran (or on an object without it): fall back to the
+    # structural sources, never to "user".
+    try:
+        return classify(agent)
+    except Exception:
+        return UNKNOWN

